  "description": "Years of production: 2014-2016\n\nDiscontinued, superseded by Gen2. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Escapade.\n\nThe original Cotic Escapade was a super-versatile drop-bar \"life bike\": disc brakes all round, mudguard and rack mounts, tyres from fast and skinny to big and floaty, and a choice of derailleur gears, hub gears, or singlespeed via horizontal Dogsbody2 dropouts with a solid mech hanger and chainstay disc mount. Built from custom butted Cotic Fe cromoly with the Ovalform top tube, paired with a Cotic RB3 cromoly fork (9mm thru axle, disc only).",
